---
title: Board Load & Autosave
---
sequenceDiagram
    actor User
    participant Router as spa-router<br/>(BoardController -> RouterProvider)
    participant Provider as BoardProvider<br/>(BoardContext.tsx -><br/>effects/useBoardPersistence.ts)
    participant Reducer as board reducer<br/>(reducers/board.ts)
    participant View as BoardView /<br/>RowBoard / BoardConfigModal
    participant API@{ "type" : "boundary" } as /api/v1/board<br/>(pages/api/v1/board.ts)
    participant Events@{ "type" : "boundary" } as /api/v1/board/events<br/>(pages/api/v1/board/events.ts)
    participant CLI@{ "type" : "boundary" } as kanby CLI<br/>(pages/api/v1/{rows,tasks,columns})
    participant KV@{ "type" : "database" } as Deno KV<br/>(lib/db/kv.ts)
    participant LS@{ "type" : "database" } as localStorage
    participant Purge@{ "type" : "boundary" } as /api/v1/cron/purge-trash<br/>(pages/api/v1/cron/purge-trash.ts)
    participant Tab as other tabs<br/>(BroadcastChannel<br/>board-sync:kv / board-sync:local)

    Note over User,LS: Initial mount
    User->>Router: navigate to "/dashboard"<br/>(or deep-link "/dashboard/row/:shortId"<br/>from the drawer's project-row list)
    Note over User,Router: On the dashboard, drawer row clicks (the data-board-link anchors)<br/>are intercepted by BoardController and routed via router.navigate<br/>client-side, so there is no reload and no BOARD/LOAD. This reaches the<br/>rowId param scroll step below. Off the SPA it is a full page load.
    Router->>Provider: render BoardProvider<br/>useReducer(boardReducer, createInitialState)
    Provider->>View: initial render, boardLoaded = false

    Note over User,LS: Load on mount (useEffect)
    Note over Provider,Reducer: boardId === "demo" (landing-page demo): dispatch(BOARD/LOAD, createDemoBoard())<br/>and nothing else — no API, no localStorage, no autosave, no cross-tab sync.<br/>If loading throws (fetch rejects, non-JSON body), it logs and dispatches BOARD/RESET.
    rect rgba(38, 240, 58, 0.25)
        critical isAuthenticated
            Provider->>API: GET /api/v1/board
            API->>KV: getBoardRevision(boardId)<br/>(versionstamp of ["board_rev", boardId], read first)
            API->>KV: getBoard(boardId)
            rect rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.5)
                alt board exists (200)
                    rect rgba(38, 240, 58, 0.25)
                        KV-->>API: list ["row"|"column"|"task", boardId]<br/>(no entities but a legacy ["board", id] entry: one atomic<br/>check(versionstamp) commit writes its entities + deletes it;<br/>conflict -> another request migrated it, re-list)
                        API-->>Provider: 200 {rows, columns, tasks} + ETag (board revision)
                        Provider->>Provider: savedRef = per-entity JSON of the response<br/>revRef = ETag
                        Provider->>Reducer: dispatch(BOARD/LOAD, remote)<br/>-> board.load(state, payload)
                    end
                else no data (404)
                    
                    rect rgba(240, 38, 38, 0.25)
                        KV--xAPI: null
                        API--xProvider: 404 {noData: true} + ETag "none"<br/>(revRef = "none")
                        Provider->>LS: localStorage.getItem(STORAGE_KEY)
                        activate Provider
                    end
                    rect rgba(240, 163, 38, 0.25)
                        break legacy local data found
                            rect rgba(38, 240, 58, 0.25)
                                LS-->>Provider: stored JSON
                                Provider->>API: PATCH /api/v1/board {upserts: local, deletes: none}<br/>If-Match: "none" (no board may exist yet)<br/>(migrate local -> remote; split into chunks of 1000 like autosave)
                                API->>KV: applyBoardChanges(boardId, changes, [revisionCheck])<br/>(409 if another tab migrated first: treated as not ok,<br/>and the first autosave then gets a 409 and merges)
                                opt PATCH ok
                                    Provider->>LS: localStorage.removeItem(STORAGE_KEY)
                                    Provider->>Provider: savedRef = per-entity JSON of local<br/>(not ok: savedRef stays empty, so the<br/>first autosave sends everything)
                                end
                                Provider->>Reducer: dispatch(BOARD/LOAD, local)<br/>-> board.load(state, payload)
                            end
                        end
                        opt no local data
                            Provider->>Reducer: dispatch(BOARD/RESET)<br/>-> board.reset() (default columns + Trash, no rows)
                        end
                    end
                    deactivate Provider
                else any other error status
                    API--xProvider: non-404 error
                    Note over Provider: no dispatch: board stays unloaded (boardLoaded = false)
                end
            end
        end
    end
    rect rgba(240, 38, 38, 0.25)
        break not authenticated
            Provider->>LS: localStorage.getItem(STORAGE_KEY)
            alt stored data found
                LS-->>Provider: stored board JSON
                activate Provider
                Provider->>LS: pruneLocalComments(keepTaskIds) (commentStore.ts)<br/>keepTaskIds = stored task ids minus expiredTrashTaskIds(...)<br/>-> drops comments of any task no longer on the board<br/>(expired, row/column deleted)
                Provider->>Reducer: dispatch(BOARD/LOAD, local)<br/>-> board.load(state, payload)
            else nothing stored
                Provider->>LS: pruneLocalComments(empty set)<br/>-> drops all comments (e.g. after a board reset)
                Provider->>Reducer: dispatch(BOARD/RESET)<br/>-> board.reset() (default columns + Trash, no rows)
                deactivate Provider
            end
        end
    end

    Note right of Provider: There is now enough data to start to initialize the app.<br />All logic above is just bootstrapping to get to this point, where we have rows/columns/tasks data.

    Note over Reducer: The step below is board.load. board.reset instead returns a fresh<br/>state (To Do / In Progress / Review / Done + Trash, no rows/tasks),<br/>boardLoaded = true.
    Reducer-->>Provider: columns backfilled (normalizeColumn: legacy<br/>boards missing pin/icon/isTrash fields), Trash column<br/>appended if missing, rows/columns sorted by order<br/>(Trash forced last), tasks backfilled (normalizeTask:<br/>trashedAt/preTrashColId = null), expired Trash tasks<br/>(trashedAt 30+ days old) dropped, tasks whose row or<br/>column is missing dropped (KV has no cascade),<br/>boardLoaded = true
    Provider->>View: BoardView, RowBoard, BoardConfigModal<br/>all re-render (BoardDataContext: rows/columns/<br/>tasks/boardLoaded changed)<br/>-> RowBoard mounts one RowSection per row<br/>(or, when rows is empty e.g. after BOARD/RESET,<br/>the empty state: prompt + inline CreateRowSection),<br/>BoardConfigModal's sections render row/column settings
    View->>View: BoardView useEffect[boardLoaded]<br/>-> document.documentElement.dataset.boardLoaded = "true"<br/>(for e2e hydration gating)
    opt rowId param present (entered via "/dashboard/row/:shortId"; findByShortId(rows, rowId))
        View->>View: BoardView finds row by id, then<br/>requestAnimationFrame -> document.getElementById<br/>("row-section-{rowId}").scrollIntoView({block:"start"})<br/>(unknown id -> navigate("/dashboard", replace))
    end

    Note over User,LS: Autosave (on every state.{rows,columns,tasks} change)
    Note over Provider: useEffect deps: [rows, columns, tasks, boardLoaded]<br/>guarded by boardLoaded === true
    Provider->>Provider: loadedSnapshotRef ??= JSON of the first loaded board<br/>clearTimeout(prev)<br/>setTimeout(..., 500ms)
    alt snapshot === lastSyncedRef (state came from BOARD/SYNC)
        Note over Provider: skip save + broadcast (prevents an echo loop between tabs)
    else local change
        alt isAuthenticated
            rect rgba(38, 240, 58, 0.25)
                Provider->>Provider: queued on saveChainRef (one PATCH in flight)<br/>diffBoard(savedRef, snapshot): upserts = new/changed<br/>rows/columns/tasks (JSON compare), deletes = ids gone
                opt diff not empty
                    loop each chunk of at most 1000 upserts + deletes<br/>(chunkChanges: rows, columns, tasks, then deletes)
                        Provider->>API: PATCH /api/v1/board {upserts, deletes}<br/>If-Match: revRef
                        API->>API: shape parse (400), then fields.ts rules on<br/>each upsert, reject-only (422 {field, error})
                        API->>KV: applyBoardChanges(boardId, changes, [revisionCheck])<br/>kv.atomic(): check board_rev versionstamp<br/>+ set/delete per entity + set ["board_rev", boardId]
                        alt board_rev unchanged
                            API-->>Provider: 200 + ETag (new board revision)
                            Provider->>Provider: revRef = ETag, chunk applied to savedRef
                        else board written since revRef
                            API-->>Provider: 409 {conflict: true} -> stop
                        end
                    end
                    alt every chunk 200
                        Provider->>Provider: setSaveRejected(false)
                    else 409 conflict
                        Provider->>API: GET /api/v1/board -> remote + ETag
                        Note over Provider: closeStaleEdit(remote.tasks) first (see Live refresh)
                        Provider->>Provider: mergeConflict(savedRef, latest state, remote):<br/>conflicted = this tab's changed entities whose server copy<br/>differs from savedRef (keys compared sorted);<br/>merged = remote + this tab's other changes<br/>savedRef = per-entity JSON of remote, revRef = ETag
                        Provider->>Reducer: dispatch(BOARD/SYNC, liveBoard(merged))<br/>(lastSyncedRef not set, so the autosave this triggers<br/>resends the surviving changes at the new revision)
                        opt conflicted not empty
                            Provider->>View: BoardProvider re-renders SaveConflictAlert<br/>(shared/SaveConflictAlert.tsx) until dismissed
                        end
                    else 4xx/5xx
                        Provider->>Provider: savedRef keeps only the accepted chunks (the next<br/>diff resends the rest), setSaveRejected(true)
                        Provider->>View: BoardProvider re-renders SaveErrorAlert<br/>(shared/SaveErrorAlert.tsx, same alert as ?unauthorized=1)<br/>until dismissed or a later save succeeds
                    end
                end
            end
        else not authenticated
            rect rgba(240, 38, 38, 0.25)
                Provider->>LS: localStorage.setItem(STORAGE_KEY, JSON.stringify({rows,columns,tasks}))
            end
        end
        opt snapshot !== loadedSnapshotRef
            Provider->>Tab: channel.postMessage({rows, columns, tasks})
        end
        Note over Provider: The post-load save is not broadcast: other tabs<br/>already hold that board, or a newer one it would undo.<br/>loadedSnapshotRef is cleared after the first save.
    end
    Note over Provider,KV: Every checked save names the board revision it was based on (If-Match).<br/>Any other write since then (another device, another tab, the CLI) means a 409:<br/>the app refetches and resends its changes to entities nobody else touched.<br/>Entities changed on both sides take the server's version, with a notice.<br/>A stale tab can no longer resurrect an entity deleted elsewhere.<br/>Other devices see the change live (see Live refresh below).

    Note over User,Tab: Live refresh (authenticated, once boardLoaded; skipped for boardId "demo")
    Provider->>Events: new EventSource("/api/v1/board/events")
    Events->>KV: watchBoard(boardId) -> kv.watch([["board_rev", boardId]])
    Note over Events: ": ping" every 30s keeps proxies (Cloudflare: 100s idle)<br/>from closing the stream. EventSource reopens a dropped one.
    KV-->>Events: current entry (on connect)
    Events-->>Provider: data: change
    Note over Provider: The connect-time message covers writes made<br/>between GET /api/v1/board and the stream opening.
    CLI->>KV: POST/PATCH /api/v1/rows|tasks -> applyBoardChanges<br/>(saveEntity = one entity + its versionstamp check, so a CLI edit<br/>fails with 409 if the app saved that task since the CLI read it;<br/>same atomic commit sets ["board_rev", boardId])
    Note over KV: Every board write bumps board_rev: this tab's and other devices'<br/>autosaves, the CLI, purgeExpiredTrash, and DELETE /api/v1/board<br/>(deletes it). getBoard's legacy migration doesn't.
    KV-->>Events: board_rev changed
    Events-->>Provider: data: change
    Provider->>Provider: refreshFromServer() queued on saveChainRef<br/>(runs after any in-flight PATCH)
    alt an edit is waiting on the 500ms autosave timer
        Provider->>Provider: refreshQueuedRef = true<br/>(the timer re-queues the refresh after its save)
    else no pending edit
        Provider->>API: GET /api/v1/board
        API->>KV: getBoard(boardId)
        API-->>Provider: 200 {rows, columns, tasks} + ETag (non-200 -> stop)
        alt an edit started during the GET
            Provider->>Provider: refreshQueuedRef = true
        else diffBoard(savedRef, remote) === null (e.g. this tab's own save)
            Provider->>Provider: revRef = ETag (savedRef already matches remote)
            Note over Provider: nothing to apply
        else board changed elsewhere
            opt closeStaleEdit(remote.tasks): a task modal is open and the server's<br/>copy of that task differs from savedRef (canonical compare;<br/>a task deleted elsewhere keeps its modal)
                Provider->>LS: clearEditDraft(editingTaskId) (task+id)
                Provider->>Reducer: dispatch(TASK/CLOSE_EDIT_MODAL)<br/>-> editingTaskId/editTaskDraft = null, taskEditModalOpen = false
                Provider->>View: BoardProvider re-renders EditDiscardedAlert<br/>(shared/EditDiscardedAlert.tsx) until dismissed<br/>BoardView: modal closed while URL is /dashboard/task/:id<br/>-> navigate("/dashboard", replace)
            end
            Provider->>Provider: board = liveBoard(remote) (sorted, normalized)<br/>savedRef = per-entity JSON of remote, revRef = ETag<br/>lastSyncedRef = JSON.stringify(board)
            Provider->>Reducer: dispatch(BOARD/SYNC, board) -> board.sync<br/>(same handling as cross-tab sync below)
            Provider->>View: re-render (BoardData changed)
            Note over Provider: The autosave this triggers matches<br/>lastSyncedRef: no PATCH, no broadcast.
        end
    end

    Note over User,Tab: Cross-tab sync (same browser; skipped for boardId "demo")
    Tab->>Provider: channel message {rows, columns, tasks}
    Note over Provider: closeStaleEdit(tasks) first (see Live refresh):<br/>the other tab saving the open task closes its modal here.
    Provider->>Provider: lastSyncedRef = JSON.stringify(snapshot)<br/>savedRef = per-entity JSON of snapshot (the sender saved it)
    Provider->>Reducer: dispatch(BOARD/SYNC, snapshot) -> board.sync
    Reducer-->>Provider: rows/columns/tasks replaced (last write wins)
    alt rows.length === 0
        Reducer-->>Provider: taskCreateModalOpen=false, taskEditModalOpen=false,<br/>editingTaskId/editTaskDraft=null, checklist AI state cleared
    else a draft's row is missing
        Reducer-->>Provider: taskDraft.rowId / editTaskDraft.rowId = ""<br/>(modal stays open with unsaved edits, Project shows no selection)
    end
    Provider->>View: re-render (BoardData changed)<br/>BoardMenu / BoardDock drop "Create new task" when rows is empty
    Note over Provider,Tab: The sender's PATCH also bumps board_rev, so this tab gets an SSE<br/>event for the same save. Its refetch matches savedRef (set above),<br/>so it only advances revRef. Until then revRef is behind: a save in that<br/>window gets a 409 and merges (nothing collides, so no notice). The channel stays: it's instant, and localStorage<br/>boards (board-sync:local) have no other sync path.

    Note over User,Purge: Daily trash purge (no client involved). Planned as a Deno.cron() on<br/>Deno Deploy, NOT scheduled yet: until then only board.load drops expired tasks.
    Purge->>Purge: check Authorization: Bearer CRON_SECRET
    Purge->>KV: purgeExpiredTrash() (lib/db/kv.ts): for each ["task", boardId, taskId]<br/>with trashedAt 30+ days old: atomic check(versionstamp).delete<br/>+ set ["board_rev", boardId] (open tabs refresh)<br/>(conflict -> task skipped, retried next run), then delete<br/>["task_comment", boardId, taskId, *] whose ["task", boardId, taskId]<br/>is missing and createdAt is 24h+ old. Boards still in a legacy<br/>["board", id] entry are migrated first (getBoard).
    Note over Provider,KV: A tab still holding a purged task can't save it back:<br/>the purge bumped board_rev, so its PATCH gets a 409 and<br/>the merge keeps the task deleted. KV boards never prune comments client-side:<br/>comments of any task that leaves the board (purged, expired on load,<br/>row/column deleted) are swept by the next purge. The 24h guard<br/>protects comments posted before their task's autosave lands.<br/>localStorage boards never reach the purge. BoardProvider<br/>prunes their comments on load instead.
